message: "If you use these materials, please cite them as below."
type: software
title: "AI for evidence synthesis: materials for the EPH 2026 skills building seminar M.8, 'Building skills in using AI tools to support evidence reviews for effective public health strategies'"
abstract: >-
  Hands-on materials (activity guide, data, prompts for chat assistants, Claude Code skills, a
  browser-based scorer) for a skills building seminar at the European Public Health Conference 2026,
  Bilbao, organised by the EUPHA Digital Health and Artificial Intelligence Section with Concordia
  University, the Leibniz ScienceCampus Digital Public Health Bremen and the Italian Society for AI in
  Medicine (SIIAM). The AI beginners track is for learning only.
authors:
